wsl-dns-forward NEWS: history of user-visible changes

Version 1.0.0 (2026-11-07)

* Answers A queries for .local names through a Windows PowerShell helper that sends mDNS from every real
  network adapter. AAAA queries get an empty answer, so programs use IPv4.
* Names are refreshed before they expire and looked up again before an expired one is answered. The last
  good address is kept on disk and used when a lookup fails.
* Upstream DNS servers come from /etc/resolv.conf, the WSL gateway and the Windows 11 DNS tunnel address, and
  the server that answered last is tried first.
* A slow lookup never blocks other clients.
* Runs as an unprivileged user after opening port 53. With -D, a supervisor restarts the worker if it dies.
* Diagnostics have stable IDs with a cause and a suggested fix, documented in wsl-dns-forward(8).
